# Vampire Count, the February head (ticket 45): a pale gaunt face with a hooked nose, slicked-back black hair with a widow's peak, red eyes
# under slanted brows, a snarl with two giant fangs, pointed ears, and the high collar of his cape (black outside, red inside) standing up
# behind and beside the head. About a third of a metre across and half a metre tall, twice a human head, so it reads at range: white face
# against black hair and collar.
# Frame (the soldier's head_top socket, ticket 43): the origin is the socket, 1.815 m over the soles; the head faces +Z, +Y is up. The
# size and the height come from the head part (content/parts/vampire_head.sdf): normalized to the common size, the chin 4 cm lower than
# phase 1's (at 1.525 m, over the neck's top at 1.569 whose stub is inside it). The head turns on the Head bone, 0.25 m under the origin.
# The eyes are the small eye part monster_eye_red, meshed once, used twice.
format 1

# No collider (the hit shape of the head is a number in the registry), and never culled before 200 m: the head is what reads at range
collider none
cull 200

Detail detail=0.526
    Part part=vampire_head
